IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nt-provisions`

-- The cross-references of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): one row per reference.
--
-- Two kinds of row.
-- A row of the first kind is a reference from one provision of this text to another provision of this text:
-- the citing provision, the words of the citation as printed (a non-breaking space is written as a space), the identifier cited, and the heading of the cited provision as the text prints it.
-- A row of the second kind is a reference to another Act or instrument: the citing provision, the words as printed, the instrument and the provision as printed.
-- Rows of the second kind are not resolved here.
--
-- The script that finds them reads the text file. It scans lines 149 to 962 for
--   "section N..." (with its subsections, paragraphs and lists such as "sections 11, 12, 14 and 15"),
--   "subsection (N)..." and "paragraph (x)..." (read as sections 53(3) and 53(4) read them: as a subsection or paragraph of the section or subsection in which the reference stands),
--   "Part N of the Schedule", "this Part" and "this Division",
--   and the headers of the examples and notes ("Example for subsection (2)(c)"), which cite the provision they belong to.
-- A reference followed by "of the <name of an Act>" is a row of the second kind.
-- Instruments named without a provision are found from a list of the names the text uses and are rows of the second kind with an empty provision.
-- "this section", "this Act" and the generic words "a Part, section or Schedule" of section 53 are not references to another provision and have no row.
-- The example under section 24A that speaks of "sections 56 to 60" illustrates a range of section numbers in another Act and has no row.

DECLARE `Cross reference` HAS
    `citing provision`                IS A STRING
    `words as printed`                IS A STRING
    `cited identifier`                IS A STRING
    `heading of the cited provision`  IS A STRING
    `line in the text file`           IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Reference to another instrument` HAS
    `citing provision`    IS A STRING
    `words as printed`    IS A STRING
    `instrument`          IS A STRING
    `provision`           IS A STRING
    `line in the text file` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN r IS A `Cross reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cross reference resolves` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision printed as` (r's `cited identifier`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `heading` EQUALS r's `heading of the cited provision`

